        {
          "review_id": "R2KL1C1XQIWCU6",
          "rating": 4.0,
          "title": "Cheap and cheerful (when you get the good ones so read the edit)",
          "body": "A lot of contrasting reviews for these towels. I wasn't expecting much for the price, but honestly, they exceeded my expectations. First, I don't know about other reviews complaining about the size or weight, but the ones I received are exactly as described and pictured. The weave is heavy, 600 gsm, probably 2 300 gsm layers stuck together as the sides are different colors, but I am not so sure to be honest, there isn't any play between layers. The pile is very low however, so they're more suited for buffing an already clean surface, but there isn't much depth to trap the dirt and you could end up scratching the surface if very dirty. Label says 80/20 polyester/polyamide but I am going to take that with a grain of salt, they feel more like 100% polyester to me. Haven't washed them yet but I have no reason to believe they will fall apart, they look well made. I doubt I'll be using them on my paint, but I'll definitely be using them for the wheels, interior, leather, etc if the lint isn't excessive. If you are looking for high quality microfibers, you should definitely look elsewhere but if you are looking for something cheap for simple jobs, these are definitely ok. EDIT: It's very frustrating when you order the same items 3 times and receive different items each time depending on stock and seller (All 3 times the items were fulfilled by Amazon). My first two orders of these towels I received very similar towels (though not identical as the tags were different). Today I received my third order and the towels are completely different this time. They are a LOT thinner and are a cheap almost waterproof polyester blend that has nothing to do with microfiber. I am glad I only ordered 2 this time because these will end up in the kitchen or around the house if not in garbage (they are THAT bad). I could return them of course, but I wouldn't be bothered over 30 pounds. I know it's hard for Amazon to control generic items but I am sure they have the means to weigh the items they fulfill before accepting the stock. Avoid the towels sold by عبدالرحمن الشيمى when you order and keep in mind you will receive different towels depending on the seller and their stock which also explains the contrasting reviews you'll find for these towels.",
